Table 2 shows the quality assessment of each meta-analysis. Generally, the meta-analyses were of high quality, although all meta-analyses did not report some of the AMSTAR items, and some of the methods used in 3 meta-analyses [19] , [21] , [22] were of uncertain validity. Reporting of AMSTAR items was less common in the 2 patient-level meta-analyses [20] , [22] .

